#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0543 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), AVALCA1N(Num). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 1`. AVALCA1N is declared, AVALCAT1 is NOT a column of the table at all - that absence is the violation. Wildcard: `AVALCAyN` matches AVALCA1N so the tuple y=1 is seeded; `AVALCATy` has no matching column and its concrete name AVALCAT1 is synthesised as absent, giving the single expansion `var_exists('AVALCA1N') and not var_exists('AVALCAT1')` = TRUE. Presence Check -> dataset granularity -> exactly ONE violation."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt nameOnly=AVALCA1N
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVALCA1N type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 1
